<!-- HEADER -->
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Schema 0.4</p>
    <h1>The .media.prompt format</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A <code>.media.prompt</code> file is declarative YAML. One file describes one asset:
      what to generate, at what quality, for which output formats, and what "correct" looks
      like. The name before the extension becomes the output filename.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- MINIMAL -->
<section class="section" id="minimal">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <h2>Start minimal</h2>
      <p>
        Two required blocks: the prompt and the output. Omit <code>service:</code> and the
        tool selects a provider from the quality tier — you describe intent, not vendors.
      </p>
      <ul class="check-list" role="list">
        <li><code>quality:</code> low | medium | high drives provider selection</li>
        <li><code>negative:</code> exclusions travel with every attempt</li>
        <li>Dimensions and aspect ratio are declared, not guessed</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="code-panel">
{%raw}<pre><code><span class="c"># logo.media.prompt</span>
schema: <span class="s">"0.4"</span>
id: logo-001
type: image
quality: medium            <span class="c"># low | medium | high</span>

prompt:
  text: <span class="s">"Minimal geometric logomark, blue hexagons on dark background"</span>
  negative: <span class="s">"realistic, photographic, text"</span>

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1024
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: <span class="s">"1:1"</span></code></pre>{/raw}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FULL EXAMPLE -->
<section class="section section-alt" id="full">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Then grow up</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      The same schema carries attachments, dependency references, multi-format output,
      post-processing, and eval criteria. Here's a landing-page hero that consumes a sibling
      asset:
    </p>
    <div class="code-panel wide">
{%raw}<pre><code><span class="c"># hero-page.media.prompt</span>
schema: <span class="s">"0.4"</span>
id: hero-page-001
type: image
quality: high

depends_on:
  - ref: logo-001
    as: logo
    collapse: file

attachments:
  - path: ./refs/brand-palette.png
    role: style
    description: <span class="s">"Match these brand colors"</span>

prompt:
  text: <span class="s">"SaaS landing page hero with logo in the nav bar, dark gradient, floating 3D shapes"</span>
  negative: <span class="s">"wireframe, cluttered, light theme"</span>
  provider_options:
    safety_filter_level: BLOCK_MEDIUM_AND_ABOVE

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      quality: 100
    - format: webp
      quality: 85
  dimensions:
    width: 1440
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: <span class="s">"16:10"</span>

post_processing:
  - action: resize
    params:
      width: 1200
      height: 750
      fit: cover

tags: [hero, landing]
product_targets: [hero-image, og-card]

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  required_pass: [relevance]
  criteria:
    relevance:
      weight: 3
      description: <span class="s">"Matches SaaS landing page intent"</span>
    composition:
      weight: 2
      description: <span class="s">"Clear visual hierarchy"</span>
    technical:
      weight: 2
      description: <span class="s">"Sharp, correct dimensions"</span>
  reject_if:
    - <span class="s">"obvious AI artifacts"</span></code></pre>{/raw}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- DEPENDENCIES -->
<section class="section" id="dependencies">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Dependencies resolve as a DAG</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      <code>depends_on</code> entries name a sibling asset by <code>id</code> and bind it to
      an alias. The engine parses, resolves tiers (cycles abort), generates in dependency
      order, and substitutes the alias into the prompt — as a file attachment, inline data,
      or context, per <code>collapse:</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="benefit-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>File</h3>
        <p><code>collapse: file</code> attaches the generated asset as an input file for image-to-image style reuse.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Inline</h3>
        <p><code>collapse: inline</code> splices the asset's content into the prompt text.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Context</h3>
        <p><code>collapse: context</code> passes a description of the asset for style/subject guidance.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- EVAL -->
<section class="section section-alt" id="eval">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <h2>Make "good" a number</h2>
      <p>
        The <code>eval</code> block grades each candidate against weighted criteria (scored
        0–10, normalized to a 0–1 pass threshold) with required passes and reject-if rules.
        Failing grades trigger fallback to the next provider in the tier ladder — the best
        attempt is kept with a warning if nothing passes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Combined with <code>-n 3</code> variants, you get a cheap selection loop: generate
        candidates, let your own criteria pick the winner.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="code-panel">
{%raw}<pre><code>eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  criteria:
    relevance:
      weight: 3
      description: <span class="s">"Hexagon motif, logo-style composition"</span>
    technical:
      weight: 3
      description: <span class="s">"Clean edges, no artifacts"</span>
  reject_if:
    - <span class="s">"contains text or letterforms"</span></code></pre>{/raw}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- OUTPUT NAMING -->
<section class="section" id="naming">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Predictable output naming</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Outputs land next to the prompt file. Variants and formats get deterministic suffixes:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Input</th><th>Variants</th><th>Outputs</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>hero.media.prompt</code> (png)</td><td>1</td><td><code>hero.png</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>hero.media.prompt</code> (png)</td><td>3</td><td><code>hero.png</code>, <code>hero.2.png</code>, <code>hero.3.png</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>hero.media.prompt</code> (png, webp)</td><td>2</td><td><code>hero.png</code>, <code>hero.2.png</code>, <code>hero.webp</code>, <code>hero.2.webp</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Per-format <code>filename:</code> overrides rename any output. Existing files are skipped unless you pass <code>--force</code>.</p>
    <div class="cta-row center">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/getting-started">Try it</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
